message: "If you use this research, please cite it as below."
title: "UNIRA — One Humanity, One Future: open research, models and data"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "UNIRA project contributors"
date-released: 2026-11-04
version: "9.1"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nova-ai-company/unira-one-earth"
url: "https://nova-ai-company.github.io/unira-one-earth/"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible models, frozen data and documents testing whether a proposed one-world cooperative economy (UNIRA)
  is physically feasible under stated assumptions. Authorship disclosure: the design rules, decisions and
  research questions are the human author's; the models, code, documents and evidence files were drafted with an
  AI assistant (Anthropic Claude, models Opus and Fable) under the author's direction, between 3 and 4 November 2026,
  and have not yet been independently peer reviewed. See README.md, "How this research was made", and
  v77/review/SELF_AUDIT_2026-11-04.md.
keywords:
  - post-growth economics
  - working time reduction
  - needs-based allocation
  - input-output analysis
  - decent living standards
  - global governance
  - conflict prevention
